{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile","id":548648,"title":"[Beast] Should Nightmares be more versatile?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-10T08:37:36-07:00","id":548648,"title":"[Beast] Should Nightmares be more versatile?","content":"Nightmares as they are now are mostly limited to influencing another person's mind. It makes it rather difficult to create Kinship Nightmare that can really evoke a sense of being related to the Kin they're supposed to emulate; for example, I think a Beast may have a hard time persuading a Mage that You are Better than Them is based on some mystical familial bond they're supposed to share.<br /> Would it hurt the game if Nightmare were more able to truly affect reality, let's say at the Satiety expenditure level, in order to better emulate the powers of other creatures?<br /> For example, the Satiety expenditure level of Bugs Everywhere! could manifest real bugs, or Death is a Prison could send the victim in Twilight.<br /> What do you think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:45:39-07:00","id":548696,"title":"","content":"Beasts aren't out to prove they're better than anyone though.<br /> <br /> Also, the specificity and somewhat ...focused nature of the power base is what allows for Kingship Nightmares to work as a narrative tool of the players.<br /> <br /> Finally, Nightmares <i>can</i> affect reality, but they are the more subtle power of the two sets, meant to allow covert and social actions far more. On top of that, Nightmares affecting reality is kind of an external momentary mage thing-you're convincing other people soul deep that something is happening, and the overcharged cycle can occasioanlly allow for those souls to make change. But considering the metaphysical doohickery of all that, It should probably be a rarity within the Satiety expenditure realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:47:13-07:00","id":548702,"title":"","content":"Beast powers, in terms of the dice numbers, are immensely powerful as they are, and honestly, if they were made more versatile, they'd be too powerful.<br /> <br /> Of course, considering that that's what the mages do by default, the word 'should' really is a weak term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:52:37-07:00","id":548735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548696#post548696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts aren't out to prove they're better than anyone though.<br /> <br /> Also, the specificity and somewhat ...focused nature of the power base is what allows for Kingship Nightmares to work as a narrative tool of the players.<br /> <br /> Finally, Nightmares <i>can</i> affect reality, but they are the more subtle power of the two sets, meant to allow covert and social actions far more. On top of that, Nightmares affecting reality is kind of an external momentary mage thing-you're convincing other people soul deep that something is happening, and the overcharged cycle can occasioanlly allow for those souls to make change. But considering the metaphysical doohickery of all that, It should probably be a rarity within the Satiety expenditure realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about being better; indeed the mechanical effects don't have to be more powerful, just more real. A 2 dices penalty ould remain a 2 dices penalty, it just would be cause by a physical impediment rather than a psychosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:01:16-07:00","id":548748,"title":"","content":"I need a drunk tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:19:06-07:00","id":548789,"title":"","content":"An other example to precise my thought:<br /> Would a Nightmare be overpowered or anti-thematic if instead of making you believe your house was haunted, actually summoned a ghost there, even if the mechanical effects were the same?<br /> If yes, is it something that could be solved, or is the idea inherently flawed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:46:35-07:00","id":548819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548789#post548789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An other example to precise my thought:<br /> Would a Nightmare be overpowered or anti-thematic if instead of making you believe your house was haunted, actually summoned a ghost there, even if the mechanical effects were the same?<br /> If yes, is it something that could be solved, or is the idea inherently flawed?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it only Temporarily summoned it then i can see it as Semi-ok Aslong as it's only for the Scene it's cast/used. (Probably as a Side Effect of Satiety Expenditure AND High Satiety, With a Exceptional Success.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:51:37-07:00","id":548836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548819#post548819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it only Temporarily summoned it then i can see it as Semi-ok Aslong as it's only for the Scene it's cast/used. (Probably as a Side Effect of Satiety Expenditure AND High Satiety, With a Exceptional Success.)</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but what exactly bothers you in the power a described?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:00:08-07:00","id":548841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548836#post548836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but what exactly bothers you in the power a described?</div> </div> </div> </div>More the Implication that the Beast CAN TEAR A SOUL OUT OF THE UNDERWORLD for a Period without the Souls/Ghosts permission. Frankly that's Terrifying..... And likely too not make many friends of/with other supernaturals when they realise you can do it. Hence only for one Scene. If you could just do it and make it Permanant then.. Shit, 90% of the others will be coming for you for one reason or another...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:03:23-07:00","id":548864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548841#post548841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More the Implication that the Beast CAN TEAR A SOUL OUT OF THE UNDERWORLD for a Period without the Souls/Ghosts permission. Frankly that's Terrifying..... And likely too not make many friends of/with other supernaturals when they realise you can do it. Hence only for one Scene. If you could just do it and make it Permanant then.. Shit, 90% of the others will be coming for you for one reason or another...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't Demons do that if they want to bring someone back to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:09:35-07:00","id":548899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548864#post548864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't Demons do that if they want to bring someone back to life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not got Demon.. so can't say But I don't mind that so Much... Since Demons are Unnatural creations of the God Machine that's Breaking the Rules they have been Given. They can do things that Aren't Natural, so i see that as Fine. Beast on the other hand... Aren't &quot;Apart from&quot; the world around them. If they can open a gate for a Ghost too Come though.. that's one thing, but dragging them though without any form of prior interaction would be a No-no in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:17:56-07:00","id":548939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548841#post548841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More the Implication that the Beast CAN TEAR A SOUL OUT OF THE UNDERWORLD for a Period without the Souls/Ghosts permission. Frankly that's Terrifying..... And likely too not make many friends of/with other supernaturals when they realise you can do it. Hence only for one Scene. If you could just do it and make it Permanant then.. Shit, 90% of the others will be coming for you for one reason or another...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of ghosts in the material world, they're eve supposed to be the most commonly encountered supernatural criters. I see your point about limited duration, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:55:16-07:00","id":549132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=548864#post548864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't Demons do that if they want to bring someone back to life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. I assume we're talking the Unchained here, so if you meant the Fallen disregard this post. With the Unchained's Raise the Dead exploit the logic is that the soul is still hanging around ,presumably this is being used shortly after death and not months, so the idea is that you're making the body work again and then opening the door to let the soul step inside again. The actual botch description works off the idea that if the soul has moved on, or doesn't want to come back then the channel is co-opted and something else steps in with the most extreme being that you accidentally invited something that really shouldn't be here into the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:16:03-07:00","id":554099,"title":"","content":"It should be pointed out that, to a Mage, a Beast can totally show them what they are. Remember, their Atavisms actually have a visual aspect to them when witnessed by someone with even the smallest bit of supernatural power, i.e. when he blows fire, they're seen as an actual dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:20:55-07:00","id":554139,"title":"","content":"Do I think that Nightmares should mimic other supernaturals more? No, I really don't. At the heart of the matter, even if it didn't make Beasts more powerful, it would dilute their themes. Beasts are literally living Nightmares. How does pulling an actual ghost out of the Underworld relate to being a literal living nightmare? Should Beasts be able to drink blood? Turn into wolves? Scrutinize and analyze magic? <br /> <br /> Beasts aren't Unchained - while the latter do want to infiltrate other supernaturals by disguising themselves as said supernatural and sometimes mimic the powers, Beasts don't want to do that at all. They're not trying to be like another super. They are trying to hang out with family. Family members aren't identical. Beast would be the Mom of the family, Mage the kid who went to college, Vamp the party girl who hits all the clubs and never settles, Wolf the nature fanatic of the family, Changeling the prodigal son that moved away then came back, Prommie the weird aunt adopted into the family, etc. They're all markedly different. They don't want to be the same, they don't try to be. But they're still family. They're united by shared experiences, not shared talents.<br /> <br /> Beasts want to play and hang out with everyone, see how they're doing. They don't want to actually BE the others, though. Every game has its themes, and, while Beast's themes involve crossover, it does not involve mimicry or absorption. It involves being a the embodiment of fear. <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> On a semi-related, but small tangent, can someone tell me what the default duration of Nightmares are? I can't find it anywhere. Some powers, its obvious what the duration is, or the power specifically says how long it lasts. Others (notably You Are Meat) references the duration of the Nightmare, but doesn't say how long that duration actually is. Anyone have any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:11:00-07:00","id":554153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast The Primordial Kickstarter Preview, Page 175</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare effects normally last one scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>There you go. Right before the Eye Contact sidebar and the Invoking Nightmares explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:30:09-07:00","id":554873,"title":"","content":"Nightmares being real would make them improperly named and inappropriate to the overall concepts. Beasts are associated with Dream. Dreams can have real physical affects, but they are totally contained within a person's mind. The fact that a Beast can pull from a dream to affect reality shows their power. The fact that dream is affecting reality makes them terrifying. See Nightmare on Elm Street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:24:36-07:00","id":554973,"title":"","content":"Nightmares affected &quot;reality&quot; is both out of theme and unnecessary. The subject of the Nightmare is being affected in reality. <br /> <br /> What would the difference between the subject thinking they were haunted and actually summoning a ghost be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:06:22-07:00","id":555101,"title":"","content":"A real phenomenon could be witnessed by other people and could occasionally open new avenues of actions. A real ghost could be talked to, one day the characters may decide to track it down to gain info, make friends, or lay it to rest. Can't do this with an hallucination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:32:08-07:00","id":555158,"title":"","content":"If it was unclear, I was saying the dream affects reality specific to the victim. That is the way it worked in the movie. Victims had to be asleep there, but to an outsider's perspective they were seeing people slashed to ribbons without any sign of a cause. It is scarier that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:34:09-07:00","id":555162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=555158#post555158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was unclear, I was saying the dream affects reality specific to the victim. That is the way it worked in the movie. Victims had to be asleep there, but to an outsider's perspective they were seeing people slashed to ribbons without any sign of a cause. It is scarier that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But also less useful, from both a player and ST perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:21:05-07:00","id":555419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548648-beast-should-nightmares-be-more-versatile?p=555162#post555162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But also less useful, from both a player and ST perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's only less useful if the Beasts are the antagonists. If we're talking Beast PC's then it becomes <i>more</i> useful since you don't really have to worry about these things being as easily traced back to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T05:07:52-07:00","id":555486,"title":"","content":"Unless the target is killed in their sleep (possible, but sociopathic), I think its still &quot;traced&quot; back to you in that the victim does seem to associate the bad dream with you. Otherwise, why would it work with Hard Leverage? With seeing your true form? I think that victims know who's at blame here, at least as a feeling if not hard fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}